<title>UK: Britain would not accept EU tax harmonisation.</title>
<headline>Britain would not accept EU tax harmonisation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain would refuse to involve itself in any plan by other European Union states to harmonise their tax policies, an aide to Prime Minister John Major said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no question of a harmonised central tax policy being imposed on the UK,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He was commenting on a newspaper report saying that France and Germany would press for a single European system for tax and social security after the adoption of a single currency.</p>
<p>The aide said Britain was not aware of any Franco-German proposals along these lines.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7767</p>
